 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "기분 표현 (I'm happy / tired)",
   "en": "Feelings (I'm happy / tired)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "기분이나 몸 상태는 be + 형용사로 말합니다: I am happy. I am hungry. 부정은 am / is / are not, 질문은 Are you ...?입니다. 형용사 앞에 a little, very를 쓰면 정도를 말할 수 있습니다.",
   "en": "Feelings and states use be + adjective: I am happy. I am hungry. The negative is am / is / are not and the question is Are you ...? Add a little or very before the adjective to show degree."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "be + 형용사",
     "I am happy."
    ],
    [
     "부정",
     "I am not hungry."
    ],
    [
     "의문문",
     "Are you OK?"
    ],
    [
     "a little / very",
     "I am a little tired."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "English에서는 hungry, tired 앞에 be를 써요. have가 아닙니다.",
    "en": "In English hungry and tired use be, not have."
   },
   {
    "ko": "very는 '아주', a little은 '조금'입니다.",
    "en": "Very means 'a lot'; a little means 'a bit'."
   },
   {
    "ko": "How are you?에는 I'm fine, thanks.라고 답합니다.",
    "en": "Answer How are you? with I'm fine, thanks."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
